'''''Matthiola maderensis''''' is a flowering plant [[species]] of the family [[Brassicaceae]].<ref>{{Tropicos|accessdate=28 January 2019}}</ref> It is [[Endemism|endemic]] to the [[Madeira|Madeira Archipelago]].<ref name=botany>[https://botany.cz/en/matthiola-maderensis/ ''Matthiola maderensis''], botany.cz</ref> 
[[File:Matthiola maderensis, Jardín Botánico, Múnich, Alemania 2012-04-21, DD 01.JPG|thumb|right|150px|Detail of an exemplar in [[Munich Botanical Garden]]]]

==Description==
It is a biennial or perennial herb, up to 90&nbsp;cm height, with 5–25&nbsp;cm long, lanceolate leaves. The flowers are violet, purple or rarely white, and stand in terminal [[raceme]]s.<ref name=botany/> The flowers are very fragrant.<ref name="rareplants">{{cite web|url=http://www.rareplants.de/shop/product.asp?P_ID=6593|title=Matthiola maderensis|publisher=Rareplants|accessdate=28 January 2019}}</ref>

